<title>GERMANY: Siemens-Matsushita buys Hungary co.</title>
<headline>Siemens-Matsushita buys Hungary co.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siemens Matsushita Components GmbH said on Tuesday it would take over Hungary's Recotech of Szombathely to expand its production base in Hungary.</p>
<p>The joint venture of Siemens AG and Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd said the Hungarian plant employs 400 people and produces electronic components such as capacitors and electromagnetic impulse suppression components for automotive, information and communications applications.</p>
<p>Siemens-Matsushita had fiscal 1995 sales of 1.2 billion marks.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
